  "title": "Tu Youyou",
  "summary": "Born in 1930 in Ningbo, she worked from 1955 at the Academy of Traditional Chinese Medicine. Appointed head of her team on Project 523 in 1969, she turned to ancient Chinese medical texts for an antimalarial and helped extract artemisinin. She received the 2015 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine; a PMC article notes the credit given to one person has been disputed.",
